                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Mixed feelings about this game. I love the King Arthur with the high fantasy setting and the whole story rpg system which is really good, kinda reminding me of the old Warhammer Battlemarch game. On the other hand the controls including the camera and game stability is not great. The controls are cluncky as, you will get use to them but it is a bit off putting at first. The game itself is quite old and wasn't built or later systems which is why i suspect it crashes quite often. There are also bugs present everywhere showing the lack of polish this game had. The units in the game are to die for, the high fantasy look is amazing with heavy knights to giants and dragons there is suprisingly a large amount of units for a game of it's size. The magic system in the battles is pretty fun making the battles extremely hard at times. Maps are meh, there are certain areas on each of the maps that you can control for bonuses which is neat but most of the time isn't worth it. Story is alright nothing really special to be said about it. If you like total war like RTS you might find this enjoyable if you can put up with it's age. Otherwise I would not bother.",
